WEBVTT

NOTE week08-clip1-timeline-tokens
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.186 line:2 align:center
A hospital record is a timeline
of events at irregular times.

2
00:00:04.186 --> 00:00:08.406 line:2 align:center
Our synthetic patient arrives
in the emergency department,

3
00:00:08.406 --> 00:00:13.817 line:2 align:center
has a lactate of 4.1, gets
norepinephrine, is diagnosed with sepsis,

4
00:00:13.817 --> 00:00:18.017 line:2 align:center
and moves to the ICU three
and a half hours later.

5
00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:23.079 line:2 align:center
Codes become tokens. Ethos
splits each code into parts:

6
00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:27.604 line:2 align:center
the sepsis code A41.9 becomes two tokens,

7
00:00:27.604 --> 00:00:31.099 line:2 align:center
and the drug code for
norepinephrine becomes three,

8
00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:35.017 line:2 align:center
from the broad group down to the drug.

9
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:37.538 line:2 align:center
Numbers become quantile tokens.

10
00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:43.084 line:2 align:center
The lactate values in the training data
are cut into ten bins with equal counts.

11
00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:50.617 line:2 align:center
A lactate of 4.1 falls in the top
bin, so it becomes lactate, then Q10.

12
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.824 line:2 align:center
Time gaps become interval
tokens. Ethos uses 13 of them,

13
00:00:54.824 --> 00:00:57.765 line:2 align:center
and adds none for gaps under 5 minutes.

14
00:00:57.765 --> 00:01:01.917 line:2 align:center
Our 3 gaps of under an hour
become 15 minutes to one hour,

15
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:05.550 line:2 align:center
and the last gap becomes 1 to 2 hours.

16
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.867 line:2 align:center
Six static tokens come first, such
as sex and age in five-year bins.

17
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:13.649 line:2 align:center
Then the events follow in time order,

18
00:01:13.649 --> 00:01:19.017 line:2 align:center
so the whole record becomes
one sequence of 19 tokens.

19
00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:23.069 line:2 align:center
A decoder transformer then
learns to predict the next token,

20
00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:26.126 line:2 align:center
exactly as in weeks three to five.

21
00:01:26.126 --> 00:01:31.374 line:2 align:center
Ethos was trained on 241,000
patients from MIMIC-IV,

22
00:01:31.374 --> 00:01:37.613 line:2 align:center
and it sees the most recent
2,048 tokens of each timeline.
